@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Entitlement API
	Testing Koroneiki Account and Entitlement API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the account entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| Entitlement Name  |
	| Entitlement Name1 |
	| Entitlement Name2 |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal Six                  |
	| Liferay Version 7                   |
	| Liferay Version 6                   |

Scenario: Create account entitlement
	Koroneiki account entitlements should be able to be created.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create an account entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the account entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                     | KORAUTO                                 | |
	| Description              | Test automotive account on koroneiki    | |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField} | |
	| Fax Number               | 555-555-1234                            | |
	| Name                     | Koroneiki Automotive                    | |
	| Phone Number             | 555-555-5678                            | |
	| Region                   | United States                           | |
	| Status                   | Active                                  | |
	| Tier                     | T4                                      | |
	| Website                  | www.koroneikiautomotive.com             | |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Create account entitlements for one account only
	Koroneiki account entitlements should only be able to be created for accounts with a specific product purchase.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORENGR                               | |
	| Description  | Test engineering account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-4321                          | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Engineering                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-8765                          | |
	| Region       | Japan                                 | |
	| Status       | Active                                | |
	| Tier         | T1                                    | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiengineering.com          | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create an account entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the account entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                     | KORAUTO                                 | |
	| Description              | Test automotive account on koroneiki    | |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField} | |
	| Fax Number               | 555-555-1234                            | |
	| Name                     | Koroneiki Automotive                    | |
	| Phone Number             | 555-555-5678                            | |
	| Region                   | United States                           | |
	| Status                   | Active                                  | |
	| Tier                     | T4                                      | |
	| Website                  | www.koroneikiautomotive.com             | |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should not be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Engineering"

Scenario: Create account entitlements for multiple accounts
	Multiple koroneiki account entitlements should be able to be created.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORENGR                               | |
	| Description  | Test engineering account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-4321                          | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Engineering                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-8765                          | |
	| Region       | Japan                                 | |
	| Status       | Active                                | |
	| Tier         | T1                                    | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiengineering.com          | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Engineering" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create an account entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the account entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                     | KORAUTO                                 | |
	| Description              | Test automotive account on koroneiki    | |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField} | |
	| Fax Number               | 555-555-1234                            | |
	| Name                     | Koroneiki Automotive                    | |
	| Phone Number             | 555-555-5678                            | |
	| Region                   | United States                           | |
	| Status                   | Active                                  | |
	| Tier                     | T4                                      | |
	| Website                  | www.koroneikiautomotive.com             | |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Engineering" and the following values
	| Code                     | KORENGR                                 | |
	| Description              | Test engineering account on koroneiki   | |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField} | |
