	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Engineering"

Scenario: Create multiple account entitlements for account
	Multiple koroneiki account entitlements should be able to be created for an account.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Portal Six" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create an account entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description1 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name1        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create an account entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Portal Six" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description2 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name2        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	Then the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name1" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description1 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name1        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name1" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description1 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name1        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name2" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description2 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name2        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name2" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description2 |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name2        |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	When I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name1"
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name2"
	And I create a nested field for the account entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name1"
	And I rename the first account entitlement nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the account entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name2"
	And I rename the second account entitlement nested field variable
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                     | KORAUTO                                                                           | |
	| Description              | Test automotive account on koroneiki                                              | |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField1},${staticAccountEntitlementsNestedField2} | |
	| Fax Number               | 555-555-1234                                                                      | |
	| Name                     | Koroneiki Automotive                                                              | |
	| Phone Number             | 555-555-5678                                                                      | |
	| Region                   | United States                                                                     | |
	| Status                   | Active                                                                            | |
	| Tier                     | T4                                                                                | |
	| Website                  | www.koroneikiautomotive.com                                                       | |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name1" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name2" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

